# Engineering Standards

- Inspect the repository before editing.
- Follow existing architecture and conventions unless there is a documented reason to change them.
- Prefer small, coherent, testable changes.
- Never commit secrets or production credentials.
- Preserve backward compatibility unless a breaking change is explicitly approved.
- Validate external input and enforce authorization server-side.
- Add or update tests for changed behavior where practical.
- Run relevant lint, type, test, and build checks before completion.
- Update documentation when behavior, setup, API contracts, or architecture changes.
- Review the final diff for unrelated changes, debug code, generated noise, and regressions.
- Do not add AI co-author attribution unless explicitly requested.
